  <ym-title|Selected stationary linear data \V draft
  correspondence><label|selected-stationary-linear-data--draft-correspondence>

  Pin <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. Output SHA256
  <verbatim|2dacbb406c8c34fdde8a9a48b89e96ee8c580ec8f461e00b11f42f994f9fd182>.

  Inspected sources (namespace YM.Stationary except Rack):

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|Shape/Vertex.lean>: Headers.cruise, launchBridge. Fourier
    evaluation and forwardC commute including centered carry. Canonical
    free-kernel-estimates theorem thm:ex-lattice-wire-tower-strip e1
    s\<less\>=2 and retained horizon unchanged A0 supply exact powers.

    <item><verbatim|Level/Recurse.lean>: hull_fact, tack_columns; uses
    Craft.Rack.legs and Bid.Retained equalities, paces_extend, schedule
    admissibility. <verbatim|Level/Transition.lean>: actual
    Scud.legs\<rightarrow\>Cruise Phi 2 w0 D.

    <item><verbatim|Joint/Regulator.lean>: rocket/indexX/cannonade,
    rocket_root, carries, count_ammo, missile, arsenal. Gauge frame ratio
    gives negative logarithm identity, then X gauge=I. Regulator definitions
    tonic/ammo/pebble/cannon/grenade retain \<mu\>\<twosuperior\> times ninth
    power.

    <item><verbatim|Block/Static.lean>: tailor_arch, shear_pole;
    centered/rooted coordinate consistency requires triangular derivative and
    psi_proj identity. giftQ/netY/shadeR/slabW.

    <item><verbatim|Block/Packing.lean>: spreadM, jar_travel.

    <item><verbatim|Spectral/ComplexGap.lean>: fired, ticket_own,
    compass/judge/post_cert. Same finite matrix identity extends along
    unbounded periods. Gifts actual postmark Hessian uses attached
    path/Sworn/floor at identity.

    <item><verbatim|Spectral/RealGap.lean>: Chromatic.costs (L\<twosuperior\>
    from normalized frame L2); <verbatim|Films/ThinTrace.lean>
    conquer/legion_right use regulator \<mu\>\<twosuperior\>, frame jets and
    folded scalar inverses for uniform bounds. Here only constant F bound is
    asserted, not all positive-order trace matrix charges.
  </itemize-minus>

  Canonical reuse: weighted-frame-penalty proves normalized centered frame
  jets; weighted-stationary-inverses proves regulator symbol bounds. Previous
  bridge wire theorem and retained construction reused without new selection.
  Elementary matrix Fourier evaluation/chain rule; no new literature theorem.

  Remaining: determinant matrix jets, trace-ideal relative comparison and
  actual finite-volume thermal recording/error. These are not inferred from
  constant-matrix equality. No global closure claim. Checks: targeted source
  reads and hash. No Lean build, axiom replay or source edits. Independent
  review requested.

  Independent bounded draft review passed at
  2b609a230363936a82b829102cc840ca620e3efcb12562338c27023e0ce4a3e1
  (2026-11-12 05:23 UTC). Static inverse and selected linear-data units now
  supply each other\<#2019\>s explicit interfaces; full determinant-jet and
  finite-volume recording estimates remain separate obligations. No fresh
  Lean build.

